MODIFICATIONS
-------------
The files here have been substantially modified from the NInfer originals
and this directory is not a redistribution of that project. As of
2026-08-31, measured against the upstream snapshot:

  * 221 source files have no NInfer counterpart at all; they were written
    for surogate. Whole subsystems are among them, including the
    Qwen3.8-Flash-Next target, hyper-connections, the n-gram PLE memory,
    the TRT-LLM cutlass MoE path, host expert offload, and the vision
    tower's geometry generalisation.
  * 259 files derived from NInfer have been modified, 16 of them past
    half their lines.
  * 106 upstream files were removed.
  * 232 files remain byte-identical to their NInfer originals, chiefly
    the row-split quantised GEMM kernels under ops/linear and parts of
    ops/linear_attention.

Every identifier the engine owns was renamed ninfer -> sinfer on
2026-08-31 (namespace, macros, build targets, the artifact magic and the
.sinfer extension). That rename is surogate's; NInfer's name is retained
in this file, in LICENSE.ninfer, and wherever provenance is discussed,
because it names their work rather than ours.

The divergence history is PATCHES.md, which continues as the serve
engineering log.

LAYOUT
------
As of 2026-08-26 the code lives here directly as first-class surogate
source (the former vendor and sub-project layouts are dropped): engine
modules sit under csrc/src/serve/<module>, the public API under
csrc/src/serve/api, executables under cli/ and server/, C++ tests and
benches under csrc/src/testing/serve, and the Python conversion/parity
tooling under surogate/serve/tools. Targets are defined by the main
csrc/CMakeLists.txt.

OTHER THIRD-PARTY CODE
----------------------
Third-party code under third_party/ (each with its own license):
  cpp-httplib (MIT), nlohmann/json (MIT), utf8proc (MIT-style).
The NVFP4 GEMM instantiation recipe follows flashinfer
(Apache-2.0) and builds against cutlass (BSD-3-Clause) headers.
